## Context
Second audit pass after the wave-1 raid (#124/#125/#126 merged) surfaced
5 additional test-coverage items, mostly around code paths NOT exercised
by the first round's added tests. Smaller in scope than 0120.

## Items
1. **No test asserts main.go dispatch ↔ commands registry sync**: adding
   a command to `commandEntry` in helptext.go but forgetting the
   `switch` case in main.go fails silently. Add an automated check
   (Go test that walks both and compares) — `src/go/main.go:144`,
   `src/go/helptext.go:15`.
2. **`filepath.Clean(ticketDir)` regression untested**: PR #126 added
   defensive cleaning for trailing-slash args; no test exercises
   `erg archive tickets/` vs `erg archive tickets` — `src/go/archive.go:48`,
   `tests/test_archive.sh`.
3. **`manualPreamble` build-stamp substitution untested**: PR #126's
   `%s` placeholder for the build-stamp line isn't asserted; tests only
   check the H1 header — `src/go/main.go:119`, `tests/test_help.sh:121-127`.
4. **Fixture rename + assertion tightening**:
   `0001-missing-required.erg` is actually missing-Author. Rename to
   `0001-missing-author.erg` and tighten the `wantSubstr` from generic
   `"required header"` to `"Author"` — `src/go/testdata/invalid/0001-missing-required.erg`,
   `src/go/validate_test.go:378`.
5. **`folderClosure` and `strayGoSource` have no Go unit tests**:
   surfaced while auditing the `staleBlockedBy` coverage 0120 added —
   `src/go/check.go:12, 68`.

## Out of scope
- Defer-to-0117 testing items (error-format changes).
- Direct unit tests for `parseErgBytes`, `idCache`, `ticketByPath` —
  transitively covered; no concrete failure mode missed.

## Exit criteria
- All 5 items addressed.
- `make test` passes.
- New tests demonstrably fail on a regression (verify by temporarily
  breaking the relevant code).
